# Internationalization (i18n)

Supported locales: **en**, **es**, **fr**, **pl**, **zh** in `i18n/locales/`.

## Rules

- Any **new or changed user-visible string** (menu labels, hints, titles, user-facing errors, button text) must use `t("dotted.english.key")` from `i18n`, not a literal in UI code.
- Add or update the same key in **all five** locale JSON files in the **same change**.
- Keys are English, lower case, dot-separated (e.g. `menu.settings`, `hint.back`).
- Logger messages and developer comments stay in English; only UI strings are translated.
- Native language names in the locale picker (`locale.en`, `locale.es`, …) stay in their native form in every file.

## Examples

```python
# BAD — hardcoded label, missing catalog entries
yield NavAction("Settings", "settings", id="menu_settings")

# GOOD
yield NavAction(t("menu.settings"), "settings", id="menu_settings")
```

When adding `menu.settings`, update `i18n/locales/en.json`, `es.json`, `fr.json`, `pl.json`, and `zh.json` together.
